{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-115546",
  "enisaUuid": "8e4b2b38-047c-3b53-93f2-f6c09ef6977b",
  "description": "The pppoe_wrapper vendor daemon from the Amlogic Android SDK, as shipped on Nexbox A95X (Amlogic S905/S905X) TV boxes, contains a command injection vulnerability that allows local attackers to execute arbitrary commands as root by sending crafted messages to a world-writable AF_UNIX datagram socket at /dev/socket/pppoe_wrapper. Attackers can send a message beginning with 'pppd pty' followed by shell metacharacters and arbitrary commands, which are passed unfiltered to system(3) and executed by /system/bin/sh -c as root, resulting in full privilege escalation.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 2, 2026, 7:42:49 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 2, 2026, 7:47:01 PM",
